    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0851" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg565"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-23T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 23, 1916, 7 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3084. Your 3949, March 14. Mitchell-Bissell application for
                    porcelain guides and cyanide application have been pending since November with
                    constant promises of consideration. Department urges immediate reply as delay is
                    intolerable. Carefully review previous cables and press Sir Edward Grey for an immediate reply on both
                    these matters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
